+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Authenticated customers currently lose carts across sessions, cannot reliably calculate totals, receive infrastructure errors for ordinary checkout validation failures, and see incorrect order-list metadata. These defects directly affect returning customers and can cause incorrect or duplicate checkout attempts.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Associate carts created or modified with an authenticated customer and select that customer's most recently changed, uncompleted cart when no cart code is supplied.
+- Enforce customer ownership for authenticated cart retrieval, totals, and checkout; return 404 for carts that do not belong to the caller.
+- Calculate authenticated cart totals with the customer's delivery address and the same tax/subtotal/total rules used by checkout.
+- Return HTTP 400 with the expected order amount when authenticated checkout receives a mismatched payment amount, without creating an order.
+- Remove the checked-out cart from the customer's current-cart selection.
+- Return accurate customer-only order counts and page totals, ordered newest first.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `authenticated-shopping`: Persistent customer cart ownership, secure authenticated cart access, checkout validation, and customer order listing behavior.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None; this checkout has no existing main capability specifications.
+
+## Impact
+
+The change affects `sm-shop` cart/order APIs and facades, `sm-core` shopping-cart and order repository/service queries, cart persistence timestamps/status, exception-to-HTTP mapping, and focused unit/integration tests. Guest endpoints remain compatible and retain their existing validation behavior.
